config BR2_PACKAGE_KICK_CAMERA
	bool "kick-camera"
	depends on BR2_INSTALL_LIBSTDCPP
	depends on BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_THREADS
	help
	  Camera capture service for the Kick. Captures frames from a
	  V4L2 device (the MIPI CSI sensor or a USB webcam) and shares
	  them with other processes through POSIX shared memory.

	  The camera stays closed until a client sends "enable" on the
	  control socket. The service has no network access and writes no
	  frames to disk unless a debug option is set.

	  It is plain C++17 with no dependencies beyond the C and C++
	  libraries, and installs one binary, a config file and a systemd
	  unit. The unit is only installed and enabled when the init
	  system is systemd.

	  Source: Kick/services/kick_camera in this repository.

comment "kick-camera needs a toolchain w/ C++ and threads"
	depends on !BR2_INSTALL_LIBSTDCPP || !BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_THREADS
